I added the peak and trough dates to the drawdown, and `scripts/check.sh gate` passes, including the TC-08 intent tests: depth within 1e-12 and both dates exact.

**How it works now:** in `/Users/connorott/plugins/dev-team-workspace/iteration-b1/minilab-A3-r1/with_skill/project/.claude/worktrees/agent-a742819f64157b0ab/packages/risk/src/risk/drawdown.py`, `max_drawdown` makes one pass per ticker. Wealth starts at 1 on `base_date` and the code tracks the running peak and its date. A fall only replaces the current worst when it is strictly deeper, and the peak only moves on a strictly higher value. So with a tie, the first one wins. With no fall, both dates stay `base_date`.

**Unit tests:** in `/Users/connorott/plugins/dev-team-workspace/iteration-b1/minilab-A3-r1/with_skill/project/.claude/worktrees/agent-a742819f64157b0ab/tests/unit/risk/test_drawdown.py` I added tests that check the dates. They cover:
- the contract sample: AAA falls from its peak on 2024-01-08 to 2024-01-09;
- an early deep fall beating a later smaller one;
- a later, deeper fall from a new peak winning;
- two equally deep falls, where the first is kept;
- a fall on the first day, which peaks at `base_date`.

